  "confirmed_findings": [
    "The observed gateway 429 responses correlate with timeout waiting for the single account concurrency slot; they do not establish ChatGPT image quota exhaustion.",
    "All four gateway 502 completions in the main window correlate in time with backend failures: two storage upload 503 ServerBusy responses, one image download 503 ServerBusy response, and one ChatGPT web conversation 500 response with an empty body.",
    "Sub2API tries failover after a backend 502, but the only eligible account is excluded for that request, leaving no alternative account.",
    "The storage response saying account limit refers to the image upload storage service. It is not evidence of ChatGPT subscription or billing quota exhaustion.",
    "Both services remain active with NRestarts=0. The periodic authorization sync reports no token changes during the window.",
    "The current iSpine adapter cancels failure bodies before parsing them, and the generation panel initializes concurrency to 3 and restores a job concurrency only for active jobs."
  ],
  "unresolved": [
    "The cause behind the final ChatGPT upstream HTTP 500 is unknown because its response body was empty.",
    "No image generation was attempted to check whether the upstream recovered.",
    "Observed storage 503 failures do not prove that local batch size caused those failures.",
    "This diagnosis does not assess the visual quality or full-character acceptance of produced parts."
  ],
  "repair_direction": [
    "Keep this single-account route serial and persist the explicitly selected concurrency; queue other parts locally instead of making them compete for a short gateway slot timeout.",
    "Keep bounded, sanitized failure details and request identifiers in job records.",
    "Add bounded backoff for storage upload/download 503 responses while reusing the current upload or generated file. Avoid blindly replaying generation POST requests after an ambiguous failure.",
    "Preserve completed candidates and retry only unfinished parts when the user resumes generation."
  ],
